        "### 2) Single Simulation Over Time (Narrative + Plot)\n",
        "\n",
        "Briefly narrate and visualize what happens to your account balance over the course of one run. Are you happy with the outcome? Why? or Why not? You can use a time series plot to visualize the changes in your account balance over time.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Answer:**\n",
        "\n",
        "This simulation shows high volatility—the balance swings dramatically due to +50% (heads) and -40% (tails) coin flips. Early on, the balance may rise when you get a few heads in a row, but as the years go by, tails erode those gains. By age 75, your balance usually shrinks drastically.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Outcome:** Starting at $30,000 (age 35), ending at $583.57 (age 75)—a loss of 98.1%.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Are you happy with this outcome?** No. This demonstrates extreme downside risk—while the game has positive expected value, a single path can result in near-total loss. This shows why one simulation is insufficient for decision-making."
      ],
      "id": "efee057b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "message": false
      },
      "source": [
        "#| echo: false\n",
        "#| warning: false\n",
        "#| label: q2-single-sim-py\n",
        "#| fig-cap: Single simulation path of account balance\n",
        "\n",
        "# Explanation of options:\n",
        "# - echo: false = Hide code, show results/plots\n",
        "# - output: false = Hide text output (print statements), but still show plots\n",
        "# - fig-cap = Figure caption for the plot\n",
        "\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "# Set seed for reproducibility\n",
        "np.random.seed(42)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Parameters\n",
        "initial_balance = 30000\n",
        "years = 40  # Starting at age 35, playing until 75\n",
        "balances = [initial_balance]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Simulate one path\n",
        "current_balance = initial_balance\n",
        "for year in range(years):\n",
        "    coin_flip = np.random.binomial(1, 0.5)  # 1 = heads, 0 = tails\n",
        "    if coin_flip == 1:\n",
        "        current_balance *= 1.5  # +50% increase\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        current_balance *= 0.6  # -40% decrease\n",
        "    balances.append(current_balance)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create time series plot\n",
        "fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 5))\n",
        "start_age = 35\n",
        "ages_array = np.arange(start_age, start_age + years + 1)\n",
        "ax.plot(ages_array, balances, linewidth=2, color='steelblue')\n",
        "ax.axhline(y=initial_balance, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=1.5, label=f'Initial: ${initial_balance:,}')\n",
        "ax.set_xlabel('Age (Years)', fontsize=12)\n",
        "ax.set_ylabel('Account Balance ($)', fontsize=12)\n",
        "ax.set_title('Single Simulation: Account Balance Over Time', fontsize=14, fontweight='bold')\n",
        "ax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n",
        "ax.legend()\n",
        "ax.tick_params(axis='y', labelsize=10)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Format y-axis as currency\n",
        "ax.yaxis.set_major_formatter(plt.FuncFormatter(lambda x, p: f'${x:,.0f}'))\n",
        "\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Print final balance\n",
        "final_balance = balances[-1]\n",
        "print(f\"\\nInitial balance at age 35: ${initial_balance:,}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Final balance at age 75: ${final_balance:,.2f}\")\n",
        "print(f\"Net change: ${final_balance - initial_balance:,.2f} ({((final_balance / initial_balance) - 1) * 100:.1f}%)\")"
      ],
      "id": "q2-single-sim-py",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
